    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Taylor Ward** (70.58) headline the lineup as our most potent options. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from an elite matchup against Sugano, leveraging a 19% boost from the starting pitcher\u2019s poor expected ERA and a favorable platoon advantage, while **Taylor Ward** thrives on a significant park factor boost, offsetting a minor platoon dip to secure a top-tier score. **Jonathan Aranda** also projects as an elite play (70.47) due to his spot in the two-hole and an 18% boost against a vulnerable Rodriguez, R. The heavy reliance on **Lawrence Butler** and **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2014the latter seeing an impressive 68.21 score against a struggling Abbott\u2014is critical for our pursuit of category volume, particularly as we monitor for any late-breaking lineup changes.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing the 40-point efficiency floor. **Drew Gilbert** was the closest to cracking the starting nine, scoring a 38.69 that fell just short of the threshold due to a poor lineup position and platoon disadvantage against Rolison. **Bryson Stott** also missed the cut (37.68) as he continues to struggle against left-handed pitching and faces a difficult matchup against Harrison, whose xERA of 3.39 is the most daunting on today\u2019s board. We are currently navigating the absences of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Cal Raleigh**, leaving the core to carry the load. While we look for speed and production from **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Gavin Sheets** to keep us competitive in the stolen base category, we must remain vigilant regarding the platoon disadvantages facing **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Luis Arraez**, both of whom are hovering near the bottom of our efficiency range due to tough matchups against Rolison.",
